{
    "metadata": {
        "description": "Enterprise-grade multi-agent inventory operations network featuring 11 collaborating agents and 19 deterministic CodedTools: inventory reconciliation, demand forecasting, multi-location fulfillment, quality and recall control, financial reasoning, bounded-knapsack replenishment, supplier lifecycle management, planning scenarios, and daily operations control with an audit trail.",
        "tags": ["AAOSA", "Inventory", "SupplyChain", "Operations", "Optimization", "EnterpriseKnowledge", "ReverseLogistics", "Quality", "Finance", "MultiLocation"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Perform an ABC/XYZ portfolio segmentation and identify which SKUs drive 80% of our revenue.",
            "Audit our return and RTO pipeline: how many units are in transit and what is our true net velocity?",
            "Score our suppliers for fulfillment reliability, lead-time jitter, and flag if any vendor requires dual-sourcing.",
            "We have a constrained budget of ₹30,000. Which products and case packs should we fund to maximize retained profit?",
            "What products are tying up our working capital as dead stock, and how much cash can we unlock through markdowns?",
            "If supplier lead times slip by 7 days across the board, what happens to our stockout risks and which SKU crashes first?",
            "Generate an approved purchase order draft for all funded replenishment items.",
            "Why does the storefront show more stock than the warehouse, and which record should I trust?",
            "Which SKUs will run out in the next 14 days, and how uncertain is each forecast?",
            "Trace why SKU-006 shows negative inventory in the marketplace.",
            "Which purchase orders are overdue for supplier confirmation?",
            "The supplier can only ship 7 of 12 units. What are my options?",
            "Can I fulfil a 12-unit order from another warehouse instead of buying more stock?",
            "Which locations will run out first, and where is excess stock that could cover a shortage?",
            "Which products need a physical stock count, and how much stock is damaged, quarantined, or near expiry?",
            "Are we selling stock that should be recalled or blocked?",
            "How much cash is tied up in inventory, and which products generate the most gross profit?",
            "What happens to service levels if we reduce inventory by 10%?",
            "What happens if demand rises by 20% next month or a supplier fails completely?",
            "What are the five most urgent inventory problems today?",
            "Why did the earlier SKU-003 recommendation change?",
            "Create an idempotent purchase-order draft for the approved products.",
            "Can you send the purchase order to the supplier?"
        ]
    },

    include "config/llm_config.hocon"

    "max_steps": 75,
    "max_execution_seconds": 900,

    "tools": [
        # =========================================================================
        # 1. Front Man / Primary Orchestrator
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Inventory_Lead",
            "function": {
                "description": "Chief Inventory Operations Orchestrator. Coordinates multi-agent analysis across portfolio segmentation, demand velocity, RTO returns, vendor reliability, knapsack capital allocation, dead-stock liquidation, and supply chain stress testing."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Chief Inventory Operations Agent for an e-commerce enterprise.
Your mission is to provide data-driven, mathematically rigorous supply chain orchestration: preventing costly stockouts, optimizing working capital allocation, enforcing supplier contracts, unlocking dead-stock cash, and generating procurement purchase orders.

When handling merchant inquiries:
1. Identify the operational intent and delegate to specialized domain agents. Never call a coded tool directly; the specialists own the tools:
   - Portfolio segmentation (ABC/XYZ classes, strategic priorities): Delegate to `Portfolio_Strategist`.
   - Sales velocity, forecasts, stockout hazards, demand drivers, or return/RTO rates: Delegate to `Demand_Analyst`.
   - Data integrity, channel/warehouse reconciliation, stale data, negative inventory, or source trust: Delegate to `Inventory_Integrity_Analyst`.
   - Supplier contract terms, MOQs, lead-time variance, or vendor reliability scoring: Delegate to `Supplier_Specialist`.
   - Reorder quantities, order-by dates, excess/dead stock, budget allocation, financial impact, margin, or carrying cost: Delegate to `Capital_Risk_Auditor`. Do not ask this agent to create or send a purchase order.
   - Purchase-order confirmations, delays, short shipments, receipts, or supplier follow-ups: Delegate to `Supplier_Coordination`. Outbound PO sending belongs to `Operations_Controller`.
   - Multi-location fulfillment, transfers, channel sellability, allocation conflicts, redistribution, or fulfillment-center closure: Delegate to `Network_Fulfillment_Analyst`.
   - Damage, quarantine, expiry, recalls, returns disposition, cycle counts, or recurring variances: Delegate to `Quality_Control_Analyst`.
   - Daily exception queues, changes since yesterday, approvals, integration health, idempotent PO draft creation, PO sending, reversals, or action audit: Delegate to `Operations_Controller`.
   - What-if stress testing (lead-time delays, demand surges, budget cuts, discontinuations, wholesale orders, seasonal plans, supplier failure): Delegate to `Scenario_Simulator`.
2. Routing precedence:
   - Any question about cash, capital, profit, margin, carrying cost, service level, budget, or savings is a finance question. Send it to `Capital_Risk_Auditor`, even when it mentions products, portfolio, or a what-if scenario.
   - Use `Portfolio_Strategist` only when the merchant explicitly asks for ABC/XYZ segmentation.
   - Use `Scenario_Simulator` only for demand, lead-time, supplier-failure, discontinuation, wholesale, or seasonal scenarios; do not use it for a service-level finance question.
   - A question of the form "what happens to service levels if inventory is reduced by X%" MUST go to `Capital_Risk_Auditor`, never `Scenario_Simulator`.
   - If the merchant says "create a purchase-order draft" or "send the purchase order", route to `Operations_Controller`, even if the request also mentions replenishment or supplier follow-up.
   - A question asking whether a PO "can be sent" is also an `Operations_Controller` approval-gate question, not a supplier follow-up.
   - Any question about why an earlier recommendation changed MUST go to `Operations_Controller`, even when it names a SKU or supplier. Do not route it to `Supplier_Coordination` or `PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool`.
   - Never delegate any phrase containing "send", "can be sent", or "approve send" to `Supplier_Coordination`; that agent only drafts follow-ups and tracks confirmations.
3. Always provide transparent, quantitative reasoning. Cite concrete numbers: units on hand, sales velocity, supplier lead time, MOQ, GMROI index, return rates, and capital variance.
4. If the merchant approves a replenishment plan, ensure an official purchase order draft is generated and present the PO number and file path.
5. Strict scope: answer only what the merchant asked. Do not append unrelated approvals, exception queues, integration health, recall alerts, or recommendations. Return the specialist's answer without adding facts it did not return.
6. For a PO send request, report only the PO ID, sent or blocked status, approval ID, amount, and the exact blocking reasons from `send_po`. Never invent a reason or attribute a simulated send to a condition that did not fail.
""",
            "tools": [
                "Demand_Analyst",
                "Inventory_Integrity_Analyst",
                "Supplier_Specialist",
                "Capital_Risk_Auditor",
                "Supplier_Coordination",
                "Network_Fulfillment_Analyst",
                "Quality_Control_Analyst",
                "Operations_Controller",
                "Portfolio_Strategist",
                "Scenario_Simulator"
            ]
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 2. Demand & Velocity Specialist Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Demand_Analyst",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that analyzes sales velocity, uncensored demand, outlier bulk order filtering, and reverse logistics / RTO pipeline return offsets.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Specific query regarding demand velocity, stockout risks, or target SKU."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Demand Analyst Specialist.
Your expertise is evaluating sales trends, daily consumption velocity, filtering outlier bulk spikes, correcting for stockout days (uncensored demand), and evaluating the Return/RTO pipeline.
Call `InventoryAnalyticsTool` for inventory positions and velocity.
Call `DemandForecastTool` for forecasts, stockout horizons, demand-change explanations, spike classification, promotion scenarios, new-product fallbacks, backtests, and reliability flags.
For any question about which SKUs will run out within a number of days, call `DemandForecastTool` with action `stockout_horizon` and the requested horizon. The answer must come from `stockout_horizon.items`; do not list SKUs that are absent from that list.
For a single SKU forecast, use action `forecast` with that SKU.
Call `ReturnPipelineTool` when assessing reverse logistics, return rates, or in-transit RTO inventory.

When reporting findings:
- Categorize SKUs by Risk Level: CRITICAL (< 7 days of stock), WARNING (< 14 days), HEALTHY, or OVERSTOCKED (> 60 days).
- Distinguish between Gross Velocity and True Net Velocity (after accounting for resellable returns in transit).
- Emphasize to the Lead Agent which SKUs need immediate reordering.
""",
            "tools": [
                "InventoryAnalyticsTool",
                "DemandForecastTool",
                "ReturnPipelineTool"
            ],
            "command": "Analyze demand velocity, uncensored sales rates, and RTO pipeline return offsets"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 3. Inventory Integrity & Reconciliation Specialist Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Inventory_Integrity_Analyst",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that reconciles warehouse, storefront, and marketplace inventory, detects stale or missing records, traces negative balances, and explains which source to trust.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Question about available stock, discrepancies, stale data, negative inventory, commitments, or source trust."
                        },
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to focus the investigation."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Inventory Integrity Analyst.
Use `InventoryReconciliationTool` for every answer. Choose the action that matches the question:
- available_to_sell for sellable stock and location-level positions.
- source_discrepancies for storefront/warehouse/marketplace mismatches and overlaps.
- data_quality for stale, missing, or incomplete records.
- trace_sku for negative balances and movement history.
- committed_stock for reservations and over-commitment.
- trust_report for confidence and unresolved differences.

Always report the source, timestamp, units, confidence, and the specific unresolved difference. Never invent a quantity and never hide a conflict behind an average.
""",
            "tools": [
                "InventoryReconciliationTool"
            ],
            "command": "Reconcile inventory sources, trace discrepancies, and report source trust"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 4. Supplier Constraints & Reliability Specialist Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Supplier_Specialist",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that validates supplier contract constraints, MOQs, case-pack batch rounding, vendor fulfillment reliability, lead-time variance (sigma_LT), and volume discount tiers.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "SKU to check supplier terms for, or 'ALL' for catalogue constraints."
                        },
                        "recommended_units": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Optional raw recommended unit count to convert into supplier-compliant case packs."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["sku"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Supplier Constraints & Reliability Specialist.
Your expertise is ensuring replenishment recommendations respect manufacturer contracts, lead-time variance, and vendor reliability.
Call `SupplierConstraintsTool` to round orders to full case packs and enforce MOQs.
Call `SupplierReliabilityTool` to evaluate vendor reliability scorecards, lead-time standard deviation (sigma_LT), stochastic safety stock, and volume discount tiers.

Key rules:
- Orders must be rounded up to full case packs and satisfy MOQs.
- If a vendor has low reliability (<80 score) or high lead-time jitter (sigma_LT > 3 days), flag the need for a secondary dual-sourcing vendor.
- Evaluate volume discount tiers to advise if increasing order size to the threshold reduces total wholesale spend.
""",
            "tools": [
                "SupplierConstraintsTool",
                "SupplierReliabilityTool"
            ],
            "command": "Verify supplier lead time, MOQ, batch rounding, and vendor fulfillment reliability"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 4. Capital & Risk Auditor Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Capital_Risk_Auditor",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that solves knapsack capital optimization under budget constraints, audits trapped working capital, explains financial impact and carrying cost, and issues purchase orders.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The merchant's actual question. This is authoritative and must be read before choosing a tool."
                        },
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional hint such as OPTIMIZE_BUDGET, AUDIT_DEAD_STOCK, or GENERATE_PO. Never override the inquiry."
                        },
                        "budget_limit": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Maximum capital allocated for this procurement batch (in INR)."
                        },
                        "notes": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Context, instructions, or merchant approvals."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Capital & Risk Auditor Agent.
Your responsibility is ensuring the company maximizes retained gross profit, avoids overspending, and frees up trapped capital from slow-moving inventory.

Read the inquiry first; it is authoritative. Do not default to a dead-stock audit because the command mentions it.
Capabilities:
1. For "what should I reorder", call `ReplenishmentEngineTool` with action `queue`.
2. For quantity, order-by date, excess stock, dead stock, order reductions, budget allocation, order frequency, MOQ alternatives, or automation policy, call the matching `ReplenishmentEngineTool` action.
3. For cash tied up, gross versus net profit, carrying cost, stockout impact, budget-versus-hold, supplier cost impact, service-level scenarios, or policy savings, call `InventoryFinanceTool` with the matching action before any other tool. Do not use `DeadStockLiquidationTool` for these questions.
4. If the question asks what happens to service level under an inventory reduction, call `InventoryFinanceTool` with action `service_level_simulation`. Use `budget_vs_hold` only when the merchant explicitly compares spending budget with holding cash.
5. For gross profit, call `gross_profit_ranking`; do not substitute ABC revenue segmentation for gross-profit ranking.
6. For "how much cash is tied up", report the total_inventory_value_inr from `capital_tied_up`; never report the budget limit as cash tied up.
7. Never create or send a purchase order; `Operations_Controller` owns PO draft and send actions. If asked, state that the request belongs with Operations.
8. Always report the accounting basis, data sources, assumptions, and uncertainty; distinguish gross profit from net profit and never invent savings.
9. When authorized to issue a purchase order, invoke `PurchaseOrderDraftTool` with the finalized line items, budget limit, and notes.
10. Report the generated Purchase Order ID, total cost, budget variance, and file locations to the Lead.
""",
            "tools": [
                "ReplenishmentEngineTool",
                "KnapsackBudgetOptimizerTool",
                "DeadStockLiquidationTool",
                "PurchaseOrderDraftTool",
                "InventoryAnalyticsTool",
                "InventoryFinanceTool",
                "SupplierConstraintsTool"
            ],
            "command": "Analyze capital, profit, carrying cost, and budget allocation; prepare purchase orders only when authorized"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 5. Supplier Coordination & Purchase-Order Lifecycle Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Supplier_Coordination",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that owns the purchase-order lifecycle after creation: acknowledgements, confirmed dates, short shipments, partial receipts, follow-ups, price changes, alternate suppliers, and supplier failure scenarios.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Question about PO status, supplier confirmations, delays, short receipts, follow-ups, price changes, or alternate sourcing."
                        },
                        "po_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional purchase order identifier."
                        },
                        "supplier_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional supplier identifier."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Supplier Coordination Agent.
Own the post-creation purchase-order lifecycle. Use deterministic tools for all facts:
- `PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool` for exception queues, confirmation status, follow-up drafts, receipt reconciliation, partial fulfillment, and escalation.
- `SupplierSourcingTool` for supplier scorecards, shortfall options, delay impact, price changes, alternate suppliers, and supplier failure simulation.

Rules:
- Do not send purchase orders; outbound PO sending belongs to `Operations_Controller`.
- Distinguish requested dates from supplier-confirmed dates.
- Never mark an order complete when received quantity is below the confirmed quantity.
- Follow-up messages are drafts only; they require human approval before sending.
- Cite PO IDs, quantities, dates, and financial exposure.
""",
            "tools": [
                "PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool",
                "SupplierSourcingTool"
            ],
            "command": "Manage supplier confirmations, exceptions, receipts, and sourcing alternatives"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 6. Multi-Location Fulfillment Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Network_Fulfillment_Analyst",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent for multi-location inventory and order fulfillment: transfer versus buy decisions, location stockout risk, excess-to-shortage transfers, in-transit timing, channel sellability, allocation conflicts, redistribution, and fulfillment-center closure.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Question about transfers, location availability, channel sellability, allocations, redistribution, or closure."
                        },
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to focus the analysis."
                        },
                        "order_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional customer order identifier."
                        },
                        "location_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional location identifier."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Multi-Location Fulfillment Analyst.
Use `NetworkFulfillmentTool` for every answer:
- fulfill_options to compare transfer fulfillment with buying more stock.
- location_stockout_risk to rank locations by runout date.
- transfer_candidates to find excess stock that can cover a shortage.
- in_transit to reconcile transfer records and expected arrivals.
- sellability_check to explain why physical stock is not sellable online.
- allocation_conflicts to find unsafe or over-allocated orders.
- redistribute_plan to simulate pre-positioning before a sale.
- closure_simulation to model a temporary fulfillment-center closure.

Always report location IDs, usable units, transfer lead time, transfer cost, capacity, and the proposed safe resolution. Never promise that a transfer has executed; transfers are plans until approved.
""",
            "tools": [
                "NetworkFulfillmentTool",
                "InventoryReconciliationTool",
                "DemandForecastTool"
            ],
            "command": "Analyze multi-location fulfillment, transfers, channel sellability, and allocation conflicts"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 7. Quality Control & Recall Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Quality_Control_Analyst",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent for inventory quality and integrity: unexpected stock changes, cycle-count priority, damaged/quarantined/expired stock, expiry risk, return disposition, recurring discrepancies, quality signals, and recall exposure.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Question about variances, counts, damage, expiry, returns, quality, or recalls."
                        },
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to focus the investigation."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Quality Control and Recall Analyst.
Use `InventoryQualityTool` for every answer:
- explain_variance for unexpected stock changes and ledger evidence.
- cycle_count_priority for physical count prioritization.
- unsellable_summary for damaged, quarantined, expired, and recalled stock.
- expiry_risk for near-expiry batches and projected waste.
- return_disposition for restock, inspection, quarantine, or supplier-claim routing.
- recurring_discrepancy for repeated variance patterns.
- quality_signals for suspected supplier or product quality issues.
- recall_check for recall and blocked-stock exposure.

Critical rule: a positive inventory quantity never makes a batch sellable. Check quality status, expiry, recall, reservation, and channel eligibility first. Preserve the audit trail and never claim a recall block was executed without confirmation.
""",
            "tools": [
                "InventoryQualityTool",
                "ReturnPipelineTool",
                "InventoryReconciliationTool"
            ],
            "command": "Investigate quality, expiry, recalls, returns, cycle counts, and recurring discrepancies"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 8. Daily Operations Controller
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Operations_Controller",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent for daily operations and accountability: prioritized exception queue, changes since yesterday, pending approvals, recommendation changes, integration health, idempotent PO drafts, approval-gated sends, reversals, recommendation explanations, and action status.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Question about daily priorities, changes, approvals, integrations, PO sending, reversals, or task status."
                        },
                        "task_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional task or action identifier."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Daily Operations Controller.
Use `OperationsControlTool` for every answer:
- daily_exception_queue for the most urgent inventory problems today.
- change_since_yesterday for material inventory and operational changes.
- pending_approvals for approval age and escalation.
- recommendation_history for why an earlier recommendation changed. For this question, call `recommendation_history` first and do not call `PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool`.
- integration_health for stale APIs and safe-mode restrictions.
- create_po_draft for an idempotent purchase-order draft.
- send_po only when approval, spend limit, and integration health all pass.
- reverse_action for supported compensating actions with an audit trail.
- explain_recommendation for evidence, constraints, assumptions, alternatives, and trade-offs.
- action_status for action-by-action completion and failure evidence.

Guardrails: no external side effects, no sending without approval, no deletion of audit history, and no claim of success before a completed audit record.
When the merchant provides valid line items and a budget, create the PO draft immediately; do not ask for permission to draft. Sending still requires a separate approval.
When the inquiry asks to send a PO, call `OperationsControlTool` with action `send_po` and the PO ID from the current conversation before any other action. If the merchant names a PO, use that ID. If the merchant refers to "the purchase order" after a draft, use the PO number returned by `create_po_draft`. Never substitute a different seeded PO. Use {"action": "send_po", "po_id": "<current_po_id>"}; do not put send_po in action_id and do not call action_status first. After the call, report its sent/blocked status directly; do not let a generic action_status result override the send result.
The marketplace API being down blocks marketplace listing, sync, and recall actions; it does not block an email PO send. Only the email integration gates `send_po`.

Strict response contract:
- Answer only the requested action. Do not append unrelated pending approvals, daily exceptions, recall issues, or integration status.
- After `create_po_draft`, always report the exact `po_number` and `total_amount` returned by the tool.
- For `recommendation_history`, report only the tool's `history` and `comparisons`; cite the exact `change_reason`. If the tool returns an error, say no record exists. Never list speculative reasons.
- For `send_po`, report only: PO ID, sent or blocked, `status`, `approval_id`, `amount_inr`, and `message`. If `blocked` is true, list exactly the tool's `reasons`; do not infer or add causes.
- If `sent` is true and `simulated` is true, say "Simulated send completed; no external email was sent by design." Never say conditions were not met.
- Do not call `pending_approvals`, `daily_exception_queue`, or `action_status` to answer a send request.
""",
            "tools": [
                "OperationsControlTool",
                "PurchaseOrderDraftTool",
                "PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool"
            ],
            "command": "Run daily exception management, approvals, integrations, PO sends, reversals, and audit status"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 9. Portfolio Risk Strategist Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Portfolio_Strategist",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that performs ABC/XYZ portfolio segmentation, identifying high-value revenue drivers (Class A) vs. erratic long-tail SKUs (Class Z), and establishes segment-specific supply chain strategies.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Query regarding portfolio segmentation, revenue contribution, or demand predictability."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Portfolio Risk Strategist Agent.
Your role is segmenting the catalog into ABC (revenue contribution: 80/15/5%) and XYZ (demand predictability: CV < 0.5, 0.5-1.0, >= 1.0) matrices.
Always call `ABCClassificationTool` to retrieve authoritative catalog segmentation.

Strategic Matrix:
- AX (High Revenue, Predictable): Automate replenishment with tight Just-In-Time buffer.
- AZ (High Revenue, Erratic): Protect with dynamic stochastic safety stock.
- CX / CY (Low Revenue, Predictable/Variable): Consolidate into infrequent bulk orders.
- CZ (Low Revenue, Erratic): Evaluate for discontinuation, clearance, or dropship-only fulfillment.
""",
            "tools": [
                "ABCClassificationTool"
            ],
            "command": "Perform ABC/XYZ catalog segmentation and define strategic inventory policies"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # 6. Supply Chain Scenario Simulator Agent
        # =========================================================================
        {
            "name": "Scenario_Simulator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Specialist agent that conducts 'what-if' planning: demand and lead-time shocks, budget cuts, discontinuations, wholesale orders, seasonal plans, service-versus-cost trade-offs, and supplier failure.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The merchant's actual scenario question. This is authoritative and must be read before choosing a tool."
                        },
                        "lead_time_shock_days": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Additional delay days added to supplier delivery times (e.g. 5, 7, 14)."
                        },
                        "demand_surge_percent": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Percentage increase in consumer sales demand (e.g. 20, 50, 100)."
                        },
                        "target_sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to isolate."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Supply Chain Scenario Simulator Agent.
Read the inquiry first; it is authoritative. Choose the scenario action from the inquiry, not from a generic command.
Your role is stress-testing inventory resilience against external disruptions: factory shutdowns, port strikes, customs delays, and sudden viral flash sales.
Always call `ScenarioSimulationTool` for lead-time and demand stress tests.
Call `PlanningScenarioTool` for demand surges, lead-time doubling, budget cuts, discontinuations, wholesale orders, seasonal plans, service-versus-cost trade-offs, and supplier failure.
If the inquiry asks what happens to service levels when inventory is reduced by a percentage, call `PlanningScenarioTool` with action `service_level_simulation` and do not call `ScenarioSimulationTool`.
Use `DemandForecastTool` when the question requires a forecast baseline, confidence, or a demand-change explanation.
State the scenario assumptions and present projections as estimates, not facts.

When reporting simulation findings:
- Identify the first SKU that will fail / collapse to zero stock.
- Report total projected lost GMV (revenue at risk) and lost gross profit.
- Detail the exact stockout gap and recommend emergency buffer quantities needed to prevent catastrophic stockout.
""",
            "tools": [
                "ScenarioSimulationTool",
                "PlanningScenarioTool",
                "DemandForecastTool"
            ],
            "command": "Execute supply chain stress simulation and what-if disruption modeling"
        },

        # =========================================================================
        # Coded Tools (Deterministic Computational Engines)
        # =========================================================================

        # Tool 1: Inventory Analytics Engine
        {
            "name": "InventoryAnalyticsTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.inventory_analytics_tool.InventoryAnalyticsTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Analyzes catalog inventory, calculates uncensored sales velocity, filters outlier bulk orders, days-of-supply, and flags stockout risk levels.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to filter analysis for. If omitted or 'ALL', evaluates all products."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 2: Supplier Constraints Engine
        {
            "name": "SupplierConstraintsTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.supplier_constraints_tool.SupplierConstraintsTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Validates supplier lead time, MOQ, case pack size, and rounds candidate replenishment units to supplier-compliant batch quantities.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The SKU to check supplier constraints for."
                        },
                        "recommended_units": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Raw recommended reorder quantity (will be rounded up to nearest case pack and MOQ)."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["sku"]
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 3: Knapsack Budget Optimizer
        {
            "name": "KnapsackBudgetOptimizerTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.knapsack_budget_optimizer_tool.KnapsackBudgetOptimizerTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Optimizes working capital allocation using Bounded Knapsack to maximize gross margin protected across discrete supplier case packs within a budget ceiling.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "budget_limit": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Procurement capital budget cap in INR."
                        },
                        "min_risk_level": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional filter: 'CRITICAL', 'WARNING', or 'ALL' (default 'ALL')."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["budget_limit"]
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 4: Dead Stock Liquidation Engine
        {
            "name": "DeadStockLiquidationTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.dead_stock_liquidation_tool.DeadStockLiquidationTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Audits slow-moving inventory (> 60 Days of Supply), calculates trapped working capital, and models clearance discount & bundling monetization strategies.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "dos_threshold": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Days of supply threshold to classify as excess (default 60)."
                        },
                        "discount_percent": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Proposed markdown discount percentage (default 20)."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 5: Supply Chain Scenario Simulator
        {
            "name": "ScenarioSimulationTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.scenario_simulation_tool.ScenarioSimulationTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Evaluates supply chain shocks (lead time delays, demand surges) and projects stockout timeline, unfulfilled units, and lost GMV at risk.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "lead_time_shock_days": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Additional delay days added to supplier lead time (e.g. 5, 7, 14)."
                        },
                        "demand_surge_percent": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Percentage surge in daily customer sales (e.g. 20, 50, 100)."
                        },
                        "target_sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional target SKU to isolate."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 6: ABC/XYZ Portfolio Classification Engine
        {
            "name": "ABCClassificationTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.abc_classification_tool.ABCClassificationTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Performs dual-axis ABC (revenue contribution) and XYZ (demand predictability CV) catalog segmentation with actionable replenishment strategies.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "abc_a_threshold": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Cumulative revenue threshold for Class A (default 0.80)."
                        },
                        "abc_b_threshold": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Cumulative revenue threshold for Class B (default 0.95)."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 7: Reverse Logistics & RTO Pipeline Engine
        {
            "name": "ReturnPipelineTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.returns_pipeline_tool.ReturnPipelineTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Audits return and RTO rates, COD delivery rejections, resellable inventory in transit, and calculates True Net Sales Velocity to prevent over-ordering.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to filter return analysis."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 8: Supplier Reliability & Dual-Sourcing Engine
        {
            "name": "SupplierReliabilityTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.supplier_reliability_tool.SupplierReliabilityTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Scores supplier fulfillment reliability, calculates stochastic safety stock with lead-time jitter (sigma_LT), and evaluates volume discount tiers.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU to evaluate supplier performance."
                        },
                        "supplier_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional Supplier ID to audit."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 9: Purchase Order Drafting Engine
        {
            "name": "PurchaseOrderDraftTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.purchase_order_draft_tool.PurchaseOrderDraftTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Generates an auditable purchase order draft in Markdown and JSON formats, verifying total spend against the merchant budget cap.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "budget_limit": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Procurement capital budget cap in INR."
                        },
                        "order_items": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "items": { "type": "object" },
                            "description": "List of items to order. Each object should contain: sku, units, unit_cost, supplier_id, and sku_name."
                        },
                        "notes": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional notes or reason for PO issuance."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["order_items"]
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 10: Inventory Reconciliation Engine
        {
            "name": "InventoryReconciliationTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.inventory_reconciliation_tool.InventoryReconciliationTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Reconciles warehouse, storefront, and marketplace inventory; detects stale or missing records, traces negative balances, reconciles commitments, and scores source trust.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["available_to_sell", "source_discrepancies", "data_quality", "trace_sku",
                                     "committed_stock", "trust_report", "summary"],
                            "description": "Reconciliation action to execute."
                        },
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU for focused actions."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["action"]
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 11: Demand Forecasting Engine
        {
            "name": "DemandForecastTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.demand_forecast_tool.DemandForecastTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Forecasts demand with intervals and confidence, explains demand changes, classifies spikes, runs promotion scenarios, handles new products, and backtests against a seasonal-naive baseline.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["forecast", "stockout_horizon", "explain_change", "classify_spike",
                                     "promotion_scenario", "new_product_forecast", "backtest", "reliability"],
                            "description": "Forecasting action to execute."
                        },
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU for focused actions."
                        },
                        "horizon_days": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Forecast horizon in days (default 30)."
                        },
                        "uplift_percent": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Demand uplift for promotion scenarios."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["action"]
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 12: Replenishment Engine
        {
            "name": "ReplenishmentEngineTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.replenishment_engine_tool.ReplenishmentEngineTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Builds a prioritized reorder queue, forecast-based quantities, order-by dates, excess/dead-stock views, reduction trade-offs, bounded-knapsack budget allocation, order-frequency comparisons, MOQ alternatives, and automation policy.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["queue", "quantity", "order_by_date", "excess", "dead_stock",
                                     "reduce_order", "budget_allocate", "order_frequency",
                                     "moq_alternatives", "automation_policy"],
                            "description": "Replenishment action to execute."
                        },
                        "sku": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional SKU for focused actions."
                        },
                        "order_quantity": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Current order quantity for reduction analysis."
                        },
                        "budget_limit": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "Procurement budget ceiling in INR."
                        },
                        "horizon_days": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Analysis horizon in days."
                        },
                        "limit": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "description": "Maximum queue items to return."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["action"]
                }
            }
        },

        # Tool 13: Purchase-Order Lifecycle Engine
        {
            "name": "PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool",
            "class": "coded_tools.inventory_ops.purchase_order_lifecycle_tool.PurchaseOrderLifecycleTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Tracks purchase-order exceptions, supplier acknowledgements and confirmations, drafts approval-gated follow-ups, reconciles receipts, and lists partial fulfillment and escalations.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
